# /etc/qsh/qshd/config — qshd cert_index ACL
#
# Rules are evaluated top-to-bottom; first match wins.  If no rule
# matches, the `default` policy applies.  An absent or empty config
# file denies every connection (fail-closed: qshd will not accept
# any caller until the operator opts at least one cert_index in).
#
# Syntax (one rule per line; `#` comments and blank lines OK):
#
#   allow N        permit a single cert_index
#   allow N-M      permit a range, inclusive
#   deny  N        refuse a single cert_index
#   deny  N-M      refuse a range, inclusive
#   default allow  fall-through allows
#   default deny   fall-through denies (this is the built-in default)
#
# Example whitelist:
#
#   allow 72
#   allow 100-120
#   deny  105
#
# Example "everyone except 99" blacklist:
#
#   deny  99
#   default allow

# Out-of-the-box this file denies every connection.  Uncomment one
# of the rules below (or write your own) before qshd will accept any
# caller.  Find a cert_index with `show-tpm --list`.

# allow 0-9999
# default deny
